<p><strong>An online booking system is software that lets customers choose a service, a time and often a staff member on their own phone and get an instant confirmation, while the business sees every booking on one schedule. In Nepal it suits spas, salons, gyms, clinics and any appointment-based service business, and works around the clock.</strong></p>
<p>Many Nepali service businesses already take bookings through calls, Viber and WhatsApp. An online booking system does not remove those channels; it gives them one place to land so nothing is lost and nothing is double-booked.</p>
<h2>What an online booking system does</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Takes bookings 24/7.</strong> Customers book when the shop is closed.</li>
<li><strong>Prevents clashes.</strong> A taken slot stays taken.</li>
<li><strong>Confirms instantly.</strong> A booking number is returned straight away.</li>
<li><strong>Feeds operations.</strong> Staff schedules, payments and reports come from the same record.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What to set up first</h2>
<ol>
<li>Your branches and staff.</li>
<li>Your services, with durations and prices.</li>
<li>Your opening hours and breaks.</li>
<li>How you take payment: cash, card, online.</li>
</ol>
<h2>Booking is only the front door</h2>
<p>The booking page is the visible part. The value for owners is behind it: discounts that a manager approves, payments recorded against each booking and one daily report. See <a href="/features/booking/">booking management</a>, <a href="/features/payment-tracking/">payment tracking</a> and <a href="/features/operational-visibility/">operational visibility</a>.</p>
<h2>Booking vs WhatsApp or spreadsheets</h2>
<p>Chats and spreadsheets record what happened; a booking system controls what can happen. See the plain comparison in <a href="/compare/">Zennly vs spreadsheets, WhatsApp and paper</a>, and <a href="/blog/stop-taking-bookings-on-whatsapp-nepal/">why to stop taking bookings on WhatsApp</a>.</p>
<h2>By city and business type</h2>
<p>Find your city: <a href="/nepal/kathmandu/">Kathmandu</a>, <a href="/nepal/lalitpur/">Lalitpur</a>, <a href="/nepal/bhaktapur/">Bhaktapur</a>, <a href="/nepal/pokhara/">Pokhara</a>, <a href="/nepal/biratnagar/">Biratnagar</a>, <a href="/nepal/chitwan/">Chitwan</a>. Or your business: <a href="/solutions/">see all solutions</a>.</p>

<h2>Choosing an online booking system: a short checklist</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Does it work on a phone?</strong> Most customers in Nepal book from a mobile browser.</li>
<li><strong>Does it stop double-bookings?</strong> Ask what exactly is locked: staff, room, time or all three.</li>
<li><strong>Can staff use it in a day?</strong> Ask for a demo with your own services.</li>
<li><strong>Does it handle your payments record?</strong> Cash, card and online need recording against each booking.</li>
<li><strong>Can it grow with you?</strong> A second branch should not mean a new system.</li>
<li><strong>Is the price explained?</strong> Ask what is included and how a quote is built. See <a href="/blog/booking-software-price-nepal/">booking software price in Nepal</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Common mistakes</h2>
<p>The most common are choosing on price alone, copying bookings by hand between WhatsApp and the system, and skipping staff training. Put every booking source on one booking link, train the front desk for an hour, and review the first week's bookings together.</p>

      <h2>Common questions</h2>
      <h3>What is an online booking system?</h3>
      <p>It is software that lets customers choose a service, a time and often a staff member on their phone and receive a confirmation, while the business sees the booking on a shared schedule.</p>
      <h3>Which businesses in Nepal need an online booking system?</h3>
      <p>Any appointment-based business: spas, salons, beauty parlours, gyms, clinics, tattoo studios, barbershops and cleaning companies.</p>
      <h3>Do customers need to download an app?</h3>
      <p>Customers book from a web page on their phone, so no app download is needed.</p>
      <h3>How long does it take to set up?</h3>
      <p>Most businesses add branches, staff and services and go live in a short setup. Ask for a demo using your own services.</p>
      
